  "fact_notes": [
    "人物・出来事・制度は架空の教材例。実在の調査・統計・実証結果ではない。制作台帳は来歴確認用。"
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Sora, a fictional student, became known as someone willing to explain difficult assignments after school.",
          "ja": "架空の生徒ソラは放課後に難しい課題を説明してくれる人として知られた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She initially welcomed every request because explaining a concept often strengthened her own understanding.",
          "ja": "概念を説明すると自分の理解も深まるため、当初はすべての依頼を歓迎した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Eventually, her classmates began to assume that she would be available whenever they encountered a problem.",
          "ja": "やがて級友は困ったときいつでも彼女が対応できると思い始めた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A voluntary activity was gradually becoming an informal responsibility that Sora had never explicitly accepted.",
          "ja": "自発的な活動は彼女が明示的に引き受けていない非公式な責任になりつつあった。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "When Sora mentioned her increasing workload, a friend suggested that she stop answering messages altogether.",
          "ja": "負担が増えていると話すと、友人は返信を完全にやめるよう提案した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "However, silence might reduce immediate demands without communicating the reason for the sudden change.",
          "ja": "しかし沈黙は当面の負担を減らしても急な変化の理由を伝えないかもしれない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Another friend encouraged her to distinguish declining a particular request from rejecting a relationship.",
          "ja": "別の友人は特定の頼みを断ることと関係を拒むことを区別するよう促した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Sora realized that explaining her availability did not require proving that someone else's needs were unreasonable.",
          "ja": "対応可能な時間を説明するために相手の必要が不合理だと証明する必要はないと気づいた。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "She proposed a weekly study session during which classmates could bring questions and develop explanations collaboratively.",
          "ja": "級友が質問を持ち寄り協働で解説を作る週一回の勉強会を提案した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She clarified that participants would remain responsible for completing their own assignments.",
          "ja": "参加者は自分の課題を終える責任を負うと明確にした。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Some welcomed the arrangement, whereas others found it inconvenient after becoming accustomed to individual replies.",
          "ja": "歓迎する者もいれば個別回答に慣れていたため不便に感じる者もいた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The group eventually produced a shared resource that students could consult whenever the session was canceled.",
          "ja": "会が中止になっても参照できる共有資料を作った。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "During a particularly busy week, Sora canceled the meeting and discovered that other participants could organize their own discussion.",
          "ja": "特に忙しい週に会を中止すると他の参加者が自分たちで議論を開けると分かった。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Previously, she had assumed that reducing her involvement would necessarily reduce the assistance available to everyone.",
          "ja": "以前は自分の関与を減らせば全員が得る援助が必ず減ると思っていた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Instead, the experience suggested that responsibility could be distributed more widely without eliminating cooperation.",
          "ja": "むしろ協力をなくさず責任をより広く分担できることを示唆した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The revised system also provided a clearer basis for discussing expectations before either side became frustrated.",
          "ja": "新制度は双方がいら立つ前に期待を議論するためのより明確な基盤も提供した。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Generosity can become an unsustainable obligation when a useful contribution is treated as an unquestioned commitment.",
          "ja": "有益な貢献が当然の約束と見なされると寛大さは維持不能な義務になり得る。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The frequency of assistance is not the only measure of its value.",
          "ja": "援助の頻度だけが価値の尺度ではない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Respecting another person's limits can also preserve the conditions that make meaningful cooperation possible.",
          "ja": "他者の限度を尊重することは意義ある協力の条件を維持することにもなる。"
        },
        {
          "en": "For Sora, setting boundaries was not an abandonment of friendship but a way of sustaining it.",
          "ja": "ソラにとって境界を設定することは友情の放棄でなく維持する方法だった。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
